# Arabic (101) to US
# Windows KLID(s): 00000401, 00030401
# Base/Shift; Caps Lock off. No AltGr, keypad, IME or platform-specific extra keys.
# Physical positions from the 49-key Microsoft reference diagrams, including ISO 0x56.
# Blank/unassigned states are omitted; they are NOT deletion rules.
# UTF-8. Source TAB replacement. Unmatched input passes through.
# Use identity=0; multiple outputs can remain due to ambiguous physical keys.
# Example: hashcat -a 5 --stdout words.txt layouts/windows/00000401_arabic_101.table identity=0
# Use one file per run. Do not merge directions or unrelated layouts.
# Source snapshot retrieved 2026-10-07; see README.md and COVERAGE.md.
# Multi-character outputs are preserved as tokens; longest-match can hide other segmentations.
# Table-attack file; not suitable for --keyboard-layout-mapping.
# Arabic (101): https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/globalization/keyboards/kbda1.html
# Arabic (101, Legacy): https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/globalization/keyboards/kbda4.html

